Rustproofing is a must for the weapon you're going to try and finish the
game with.  Nothing more annoying than whapping something with yer way
cool Frost Brand and getting that stupid rust message.  Aargh.  Plus,
whenever I find genocide scrolls, they always seem to be cursed (I'm
from the "Awwww, go ahead and read it, it can't hurt you *that* much"
school of nethack).  Nothing like trying to kill eight rust monsters
with a non rustproofed weapon.

But I digress.  The easiest way to acquire a rustproof weapon is to have
it already rustproofed.  Organic type weapons (i.e. bullwhips) won't
rust for obvious reasons.  Also, if you get Excaliber by dunking your
trusty long sword in fountains (Valkyries and Knights), it will be
rustproofed for NO EXTRA CHARGE.  Whottadeal.  I believe that if you get
Excaliber from your diety type unit, it will be rustproofed.  Note that
wishing for it will mean that it is NOT rustproofed.

Failing that, the way to rustproof a weapon is to break out one of those
neato enchant weapon scrolls and get confused.  Getting confused
shouldn't be too terribly difficult.  Try potions of booze or confusion
(duh).  Failing that, keep munching corpses.  Eventually, one will
confuse you.  Wield your weapon, and read the scroll while confused. 
Voila!  What is it, a "golden glow" I believe?  I think it is "mottled
purple" when you're hallucinating.  Of course, blessed objects glow with
a "square" aura when you're hallucinating.

